<title>UK: FIRST BRITISH BEET TEST SHOWS 64 GRAMS SUGAR/ROOT.</title>
<headline>FIRST BRITISH BEET TEST SHOWS 64 GRAMS SUGAR/ROOT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sugar beet test carried out</p>
<p>Monday August 4, issued by British Sugar Plc.</p>
<p>			  1ST TEST   1ST 1996   5YR AVG</p>
<p> SUGAR GRAMS/ROOT	64.0	49.0	 57.6</p>
<p> SUGAR PCT		14.74     15.53	14.92</p>
<p> ROOT GRAMS/WT	    441	 316	  380</p>
<p>&quot;Analysis of the first field samples indicates that following good establishment and broadly favourable weather conditions, the prospects for this year's beet crop are good,&quot; British Sugar said. &quot;If these conditions continue it would indicate a better than average national crop. However, this is only the first sample and there is still a long way to go.&quot;</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
